{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.RhoKH3aRefinement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.RhoKH3aRefinement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rho_k_refinement_degenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rho_k_refinement_degenerate","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L192-L200","doc":"**The refinement says nothing at a Markov-trace zero.** H1 then forces the\nwhole correction sum to vanish and leaves `ρ_K` unconstrained — the content\nthe quotient form concealed inside its division. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rho_k_eq_LO_of_isLeadingOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rho_k_eq_LO_of_isLeadingOrder","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L182-L190","doc":"**At leading order the refinement collapses to the constituent ansatz.**\nThis is what the old `leading_order` field named and did not prove. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rho_k_h3a_refinement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rho_k_h3a_refinement","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L173-L180","doc":"**The refinement identity in quotient form.** Derived from the division-free\nH1 by discharging the nonvanishing of `|tr_M(β_K)|`, which is a real side\ncondition — see `rho_k_refinement_degenerate`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:rho-k-h3a-refinement","label":"prop:rho-k-h3a-refinement","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rho_k_abs_tr_M_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rho_k_abs_tr_M_pos","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L167-L170","doc":"A nonzero trace magnitude is a positive one, by H2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement.abs_tr_M_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement.abs_tr_M_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L163-L163","doc":"**H2 — the trace magnitude is a magnitude.** The `abs_` prefix promises\nthis and the type does not encode it (§3b-tax). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement.consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement.consistent","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L160-L160","doc":"**H1 — the refinement identity**, division-free. This is the conjectural\ncontent; nothing in this file derives it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement.partitions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement.partitions","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L157-L157","doc":"The partitions of `3·(Z+N)` the Wedderburn decomposition ranges over. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement.blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement.blocks","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L155-L155","doc":"Its per-block binding-fraction corrections `Δ_λ(K)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement.atomData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement.atomData","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L153-L153","doc":"The atom's categorical data tuple at `q_0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L151-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinement","kind":"class","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L140-L163","doc":"**Conditional hypotheses for the H_{3A} refinement of ρ_K.**\n\nThe class carries the atom's own Wedderburn data — its partition list and\nper-block corrections included — and asserts that *that* tuple is\nrefinement-consistent. The conjectural content is the assertion; the data\nfields are what make the assertion statable without the empty-class defect\nof `RhoKH3ARefinementNaive`.\n\nNo instance is supplied. Per §3b-tax that is what an open primary\nconjecture looks like — a content-bearing carrier with nothing inhabiting\nit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RefinementConsistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RefinementConsistent","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L133-L138","doc":"A tuple is **refinement-consistent** when the Wedderburn correction sum\nreproduces the density gap, stated division-free so that no well-definedness\nassumption hides inside a quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.not_rhoKH3ARefinementNaive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.not_rhoKH3ARefinementNaive","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L116-L129","doc":"**The naive class has no instance.** Take an atom whose density already sits\nat its leading-order value, with unit trace magnitude, unit Wenzl-bridge\nterms and unit corrections. Over the one-element partition list the\nhypothesis reads `0 = 1`.\n\nScope: this is a **structural exclusion** — the class is empty, so every\ntheorem conditional on it is vacuous. It says nothing about whether the\nphysical refinement identity holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinementNaive.identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinementNaive.identity","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L111-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinementNaive.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinementNaive.mk","kind":"ctor","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinementNaive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKH3ARefinementNaive","kind":"class","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L107-L114","doc":"The **previous** hypothesis shape, with the partition list and the\ncorrection map quantified inside the field. Kept only as the subject of\n`not_rhoKH3ARefinementNaive`; do not build on it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.blockCorrectionSum_eq_zero_of_isLeadingOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.blockCorrectionSum_eq_zero_of_isLeadingOrder","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L92-L100","doc":"At leading order every summand vanishes, so the correction sum does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.blockCorrectionSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.blockCorrectionSum","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L87-L90","doc":"The Wedderburn correction sum `Σ_{λ ∈ partitions} y_λ χ^λ(β_K) · Δ_λ(K)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKAtomData.y_chi_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKAtomData.y_chi_term","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L85-L85","doc":"`y_λ · χ^λ(β_K)` supplied by the Wenzl bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKAtomData.rho_K","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKAtomData.rho_K","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L83-L83","doc":"Full density `ρ_K(q_0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKAtomData.rho_K_LO","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKAtomData.rho_K_LO","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Leading-order constituent density `ρ_K^LO(Z, N)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKAtomData.abs_tr_M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKAtomData.abs_tr_M","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L79-L79","doc":"`|tr_M(β_K)|` at q_0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKAtomData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKAtomData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKAtomData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoKAtomData","kind":"structure","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L70-L85","doc":"**Per-atom Wedderburn data.**\n\nThe structural inputs the refinement formula consumes for a\ngiven atom: the absolute Markov trace `|tr_M(β_K)|`, the\nleading-order density `ρ_K^LO`, the full density `ρ_K`, and\nper-partition `y_λ · χ^λ(β_K)` products supplied by the\nWenzl bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BlockBindingFraction.IsLeadingOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BlockBindingFraction.IsLeadingOrder","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L64-L68","doc":"The **leading-order regime**: every per-block correction vanishes. Replaces\nthe old `leading_order : Prop := …` field, which was a proposition-valued\ndatum and therefore asserted nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BlockBindingFraction.delta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BlockBindingFraction.delta","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Map λ ⊢ 3A to the per-block correction Δ_λ ∈ ℝ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BlockBindingFraction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BlockBindingFraction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BlockBindingFraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BlockBindingFraction","kind":"structure","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rho-k-h3a-refinement.lean#L53-L62","doc":"**Per-block binding-fraction correction.**\n\nFor an atom `K` with braid word `β_K ∈ B_{3A}` and irrep\nlabel `λ ⊢ 3A`, the per-block binding-fraction correction\n`Δ_λ(K)` measures the deviation of the λ-block mass\ncontribution from the constituent-only piece\n`m_e · y_λ · χ^λ(β_K)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}